Title: A built-in empty luasteam module for games sold on Steam
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-25
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: Games sold on Steam load the module "luasteam", a native library that does not exist for AROS. Such a game stopped at start with "module 'luasteam' not found" until the user replaced the module by hand.
Change: A searcher added at the end of package.loaders answers the name "luasteam" with a built-in module: init answers true, every other call exists and answers false, a few value calls answer an empty value of the right kind (name "", id "0", level 0, language "english"). A module the game brings itself is found first and stays in use. Present in every Lua state, so threads get it too.
Scope: AROS (all targets)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64, official nightly 2026-11-24 (live ISO), softpipe (pool v1-3), 2026-11-25: a game that requires luasteam gets the module (init true, calls answer false, value calls answer "0", 0, "english", unknown name spaces answer false, also inside a love.thread); a game with its own luasteam.lua gets its own; SNKRX at 6b93a64 with its files unchanged shows its main menu, started from the package through the Workbench requester. Not run: Balatro (it asks for Steam on Windows and macOS only), Raspberry Pi.
Removal: when a Steam client library exists for AROS
---
diff --git a/src/modules/love/love.cpp b/src/modules/love/love.cpp
index fa62f4f9e0ff8604c0ee0db0041be30ac492dbd3..f3e5a69d73dd53b455f55027b73af07a835b7201 100644
--- a/src/modules/love/love.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/love/love.cpp
@@ -532,6 +532,62 @@ static void luax_addcompatibilityalias(lua_State *L, const char *module, const c
 	lua_pop(L, 1);
 }
 
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+/*
+ * Games sold on Steam ask for the module "luasteam", a native library that
+ * does not exist for AROS. This searcher is the last one in package.loaders,
+ * so a module the game brings itself wins; otherwise the game gets a module
+ * in which every call exists and reports "no Steam": init answers true so the
+ * game goes on, everything else answers false, or an empty value of the kind
+ * the real call gives.
+ */
+static const char aros_luasteam[] = R"luasteam(
+local function no() return false end
+local function space(values)
+	return setmetatable(values or {}, {
+		__index = function() return no end,
+		__call = no,
+	})
+end
+local function open()
+	local steam = {
+		init = function() return true end,
+		shutdown = function() end,
+		runCallbacks = function() end,
+		friends = space {
+			getFriendPersonaName = function() return "" end,
+			getPersonaName = function() return "" end,
+		},
+		user = space {
+			getSteamID = function() return "0" end,
+			getPlayerSteamLevel = function() return 0 end,
+			getGameBadgeLevel = function() return 0 end,
+		},
+		apps = space {
+			getCurrentGameLanguage = function() return "english" end,
+			getDLCCount = function() return 0 end,
+		},
+		utils = space {
+			getAppID = function() return 0 end,
+		},
+	}
+	return setmetatable(steam, {
+		__index = function(t, k)
+			local s = space()
+			rawset(t, k, s)
+			return s
+		end,
+	})
+end
+local loaders = package.loaders or package.searchers
+loaders[#loaders + 1] = function(name)
+	if name == "luasteam" then
+		return open
+	end
+end
+)luasteam";
+#endif
+
 int luaopen_love(lua_State *L)
 {
 	// Preload module loaders.
@@ -691,6 +747,12 @@ int luaopen_love(lua_State *L)
 	});
 #endif
 
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+	if (luaL_loadbuffer(L, aros_luasteam, sizeof(aros_luasteam) - 1, "=[love \"aros luasteam\"]") != 0
+		|| lua_pcall(L, 0, 0, 0) != 0)
+		lua_pop(L, 1);
+#endif
+
 	return 1;
 }
 
